Subject: Patient reaction possibly linked to defective batch - Fevrolix
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:18:00 +0530

Reporting on behalf of a patient (male, 45 years) who took Fevrolix tablets from Batch FVX-0091 and
developed a severe skin rash with blistering within 24 hours of the first dose. On inspecting the
remaining strip, I noticed the tablets appeared discoloured (yellowish instead of white) compared to a
previous batch, which raises the possibility that this is linked to a manufacturing/quality defect in
that specific batch rather than a typical drug reaction. Patient was advised to stop the medication and
seek dermatology consult; not hospitalized so far but rash is worsening.

This may need to be logged both as a possible adverse reaction and a product quality issue given the
tablet discolouration.

- Pharmacist, WellCare Pharmacy (synthetic test data)
